3.1 Frequently used options
===========================

   • ‘lean4-auto-start-server’ (default ‘t’) - whether visiting a Lean
     file starts the language server.  Set to ‘nil’ to start it by hand
     with ‘M-x eglot’.
   • ‘lean4-info-auto-open’ (default ‘t’) - whether the goal display
     appears when a Lean file is opened, as VS Code's InfoView does.
   • ‘lean4-info-interactive’ (default ‘t’) - whether to fetch goals
     over Lean's interactive RPC.  With ‘nil’, goals are plain text and
     cannot be hovered or jumped from.
   • ‘lean4-indent-offset’ (default ‘2’) - columns per level of
     indentation.
   • ‘lean4-indent-function’ - ‘lean4-indent-line’ guesses from the
     layout and cycles when pressed again; ‘eri-indent’ does not guess
     and only cycles, which is what this mode did before version 2.
   • ‘lean4-enable-file-watchers’ (default ‘nil’) - whether to honour
     the server's request to watch every ‘*.ilean’ file.  On a project
     the size of Mathlib that is tens of thousands of files.
   • ‘lean4-automatically-build-dependencies’ (default ‘nil’) - whether
     visiting a file may build the dependencies it imports.  See *note
     Building dependencies::.
   • ‘lean4-server-arguments’ - extra arguments for the language server.
   • ‘lean4-workspace-roots’ and ‘lean4-workspace-exclusions’ -
     directories to treat as workspace roots, and directories in which
     never to start a server.


